## 6. Worked content example — HELM -> HEADING "Planetary Survey"

### [CXC-CIC-CONTENT-PLANET-SURVEY] The reticule focuses a planet; three linked panels update from bus state

- definition: the exemplar content screen (HELM sub-tab HEADING, "Planetary Survey") and the model for "content layer, loosely drawn, masked by the frame". The `reticule` ANIMATES to focus a planet in the `star-field-dynamic` ("planet focus"); on a focus change, THREE linked displays update from bus state — `planet-image-area` (the planet image, RASTER), `planet-resources-graph` (vertical resource bar graphs, PRIMITIVE), `planet-description` (a text summary). All bus-driven: a focused-planet namespace is the single source, and the three panels each SUBSCRIBE it.
- focused-planet namespace (default STATED): `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet` — STATE, payload the focused planet's `{id, image, resources, description}` (or a planet id the panels resolve). The reticule's CENTER is BOUND to this namespace's screen position; the engine TRANSLATES the reticule to that position (the DRADIS rotation-binding precedent — a bindable transform on the animation loop, [SPEC:CXC-RENDER] / the dradis needle). The reticule is drawn as a NATIVE PRIMITIVE ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]); its bullseye/indicators are labeled parts.
- requirement: the reticule MUST derive its focus position from `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet`, not local guesswork; on a focus change the three panels MUST each update from the SAME namespace (state-on-the-bus, [CXC-BIND-PRINCIPLE]); the panels MUST render an explicit "no planet focused" state when the namespace is empty (preserve-and-flag: never a blank panel read as "no data"); and the content MUST be drawn LOOSELY, bounded by the frame mask ([CXC-CIC-WIDGET]), not by per-panel clipping. The focus namespace MUST be published change-driven ([CXC-PS-GRANULARITY]), not re-emitted every animation tick.
- default: on mount with no `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet` published, no planet is focused, the reticule rests at its base position, and the three panels show their "no planet focused" state; the reticule's focus animation eases to a new center on each focus change (the engine's animation loop, [CXC-R-ENGINE-ANIM]).
- scenario:
  - when: `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet` is published with a new planet
  - then: the reticule eases to that planet's position in the star field, the `planet-image-area` swaps to that planet's image asset, the `planet-resources-graph` bars re-fill to its resource values, and the `planet-description` text swaps — all three from the one namespace
- scenario:
  - when: a content sprite (a planet in the star field) sits at the edge of `screen-area`
  - then: its overspill is masked by the amber frame layer above (loosely drawn, frame-bounded), never clipped by the content layer itself
- scenario:
  - when: `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet` is empty (no focus)
  - then: the three panels render an explicit "no planet focused" state, not blank panes
- see-also: [CXC-CIC-WIDGET], [CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CIC]

---

## 7. Aspect + multi-instance layout

### [CXC-CIC-ASPECT-MULTI] 4:3 canon; two stacked instances on one portrait monitor, each an independent station

- definition: a `colonial_console` designs at 4:3 aspect (in-universe colonial canon). MULTI-INSTANCE: a 16:9 monitor MOUNTED PORTRAIT (physically flipped to 9:16) hosts TWO stacked `colonial_console` instances — the show's plywood "two-square" mask illusion — each an INDEPENDENT duty station with its own station scope ([CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]).
- native authoring resolution (STATED so scan-extraction + layout math have a fixed reference): the widget is RESOLUTION-INDEPENDENT — the artwork is SVG-scalable and the engine scales the design into whatever target region it lands in — but the artwork is AUTHORED at a CANONICAL native resolution of **1280x960** (2x the 4:3 base of 640x480). 1280x960 is the FIXED coordinate space the SVG scan ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]) extracts against and the layout math resolves in; a target surface scales the 1280x960 design up or down to fit. A builder MUST treat 1280x960 as the authoring/native design space and MUST NOT hardcode 640x480 or any target-pixel size as the reference resolution.
- mechanism (recommended, FLAGGED at [DD-CIC-TWO-UP]): ONE runtime scene spans the portrait display and stacks TWO `colonial_console` instances in a vertical `pixel_stack`/column, each bound to a DISTINCT `station` (e.g. `cic.1.helm`, `cic.1.nav`), so their namespaces never cross-wire ([CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION] station scoping is what keeps the two independent). Each instance renders its own 4:3 design into its region; the physical plywood mask + the region assignment crop/letterbox each 4:3 design into the square window the plywood cuts.
- requirement: each stacked instance MUST carry its own station id and subscribe ONLY its own `colonial_console/<station>/*` namespaces; a selection or focus on the UPPER station MUST NOT affect the LOWER; each instance MUST apply its OWN frame mask ([CXC-CIC-WIDGET]) within its region.
- default: a single-display bring-up is ONE instance at station `station-0` (the [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION] default); the 2-up portrait layout is the explicit multi-instance case, opted into by a scene declaring two instances with two station ids. The per-region fit (letterbox vs crop of the 4:3 design into the plywood square) DEFAULTS to letterbox-to-fit and is FLAGGED for ratify ([DD-CIC-TWO-UP]).
- scenario:
  - when: a portrait-mounted 16:9 monitor runs the 2-up scene with stations `cic.1.helm` (top) and `cic.1.nav` (bottom)
  - then: two independent CIC consoles render stacked; turning `cic.1.helm`'s console rotary swaps only the top console; `cic.1.nav` is unaffected
- see-also: [DD-CIC-TWO-UP], [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CIC]

### [CXC-CIC-ROTARY-HOOKUP] The rotary-switch hookup is a SEPARATE maker slice (pattern-referenced, not spec'd here)

- definition: the physical rotary switches (a 7-position for consoles, a 5-position for sub-tabs) -> ESP32 -> publish the station's selection index is a SEPARATE maker-project slice. It is PATTERN-REFERENCED to the dual-throttle rig (`render/examples/dual_throttle.compose.yaml`: pots -> ADC -> `publishes:` seam) — a rotary switch is the same shape as the throttle pot, reading a discrete position instead of a continuous wiper and publishing an INDEX instead of a value.
- requirement (the seam this spec fixes; the electrical hookup is NOT spec'd here): the rotary firmware MUST publish to the station's selection namespace ([CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]) — a 7-pos rotary -> `colonial_console/<station>/console = {index}`, a 5-pos rotary -> `colonial_console/<station>/subtab = {index}` — paired to its station by a `station:` config binding, so it is indistinguishable from a touch tab to the shell ([CXC-CIC-NAV]). The hookup (switch -> GPIO -> index, the deadband/debounce, the `hookup:`/`publishes:` block) is authored in its own maker artifact mirroring the dual-throttle pattern.
- default: absent the physical rotary, the shell is fully drivable by touch and by Intelligence publishes to the same namespaces (control-is-a-peer, [CXC-CIC-CREDO]); the rotary is ADDITIVE, never required.
- see-also: [CXC-CIC-NAV], [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CIC]

---

## 8. Tier scope

### [CXC-CIC-TIER] Touchscreen/desktop-first; a single console screen MAY target a Qualia (recorded stance)

- principle: per [CXC-PRIM-TIER-PARITY], a UX capability is not a landed PLATFORM capability until it renders on the embedded tier ([SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE]) OR is EXPLICITLY scoped with a recorded reason. This node is that explicit stance (the escape hatch), not a silent omission.
- stance (DRAFTED, FLAGGED at [DD-CIC-TIER]): the FULL `colonial_console` — a 7x5 CIC console with two tab rows, ambient animation, and the master mask — is TOUCHSCREEN/DESKTOP-FIRST (the Python/Skia console tier); duty stations are full touch displays. A full 7x5 CIC on an ESP32-class device is a WAIVER (the animation + two-level nav + mask stack exceed the constrained tier's budget). HOWEVER: a SINGLE console/screen (one content scene + a reduced frame, e.g. DRADIS alone, which already runs embedded via the reactive-render tier [CXC-ER-RENDER]) COULD target a Qualia-class surface. So the stance is: shell = console/desktop-first (waiver, recorded reason); a single reduced console screen = a legitimate embedded target, as a distinct reduced variant, not a claimed port of the full shell.
- reason: the shell's value is the two-level navigation + the ambient/masked composite on a full touch display; that is a console/desktop surface. A single content scene (a DRADIS scope) is a different, smaller capability that the embedded tier already serves ([CXC-ER-DRADIS-BUS]).
- consequence: the layer stack is ordinary render-engine primitives (`pixel_stack` + the mask compositing), so the DRAWING is contract-clean and a reduced single-screen variant is a back-end pass, not a rewrite; it is the FULL 7x5 shell's scope (nav + animation on a constrained device) that is console-bound.
- upholds: [CXC-PRIM-TIER-PARITY]
- see-also: [DD-CIC-TIER]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CIC]

---

## 9. Acceptance — machine signal + glass gate per surface

### [CXC-CIC-VERIFY] Two-tier verdicts — every human-perceptible surface carries a glass gate

- definition: each requirement carries a machine signal (`verify.machine`) AND, for a human-perceptible surface, an explicit human/glass gate (`verify.human`). A machine-green build with an unseen console is not accepted.

| ID | Requirement | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|----|-------------|----------------|----------------------|
| CIC-C1 | The layer stack composites in the [CXC-CIC-WIDGET] z-order; the frame masks loose content | a headless render at a given (console, subtab) asserts the 8 layers composite in order and that content overspilling `screen-area` is painted over by the amber frame (a pixel probe outside the cutout is frame-colored, not content) | on glass: the amber frame cleanly bounds loosely-drawn content; no content bleeds past the frame |
| CIC-C2 | Selecting a console swaps BOTH the sub-tab row and the content ([CXC-CIC-NAV]) | a test publishes `colonial_console/<station>/console={index:2}` and asserts `row3-tabs` = FTL's 5 sub-tabs, the content region = FTL's scene set, and sub-tab resets to 0 | on glass: turning the console rotary / tapping a console tab swaps the whole lower screen |
| CIC-C3 | Touch, rotary, and Intelligence drive selection IDENTICALLY ([CXC-CIC-CREDO]) | a test publishes an index directly (no widget) and asserts the same swap a touch produces; the shell's outcome is byte-identical across sources | on glass: touch AND a physical rotary both drive selection on a real duty-station display, indistinguishably |
| CIC-C4 | CIC state is station-scoped; two stations never cross-wire ([CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]) | a test runs two stations, publishes to `colonial_console/cic.1.helm/console`, and asserts only the `cic.1.helm` shell reacts and `cic.1.nav` sees nothing | on glass (2-up): a selection on the upper station leaves the lower station unchanged |
| CIC-C5 | A peripheral pairs to a station and publishes to its scope ([CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION]) | a test pairs a rotary (`station: cic.1.helm`) and asserts it announces at `colonial_console/cic.1.helm/peripherals/<id>` and publishes to `colonial_console/cic.1.helm/subtab`; an unpaired peripheral publishes nothing to CIC | n/a (structural) |
| CIC-C6 | The SVG scan is deterministic + preserves-and-flags unknown layers ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]) | a test scans a fixture twice and asserts byte-identical scenes; a fixture with an unknown layer name yields an unmapped element + a lint warning, never a drop | n/a (structural) |
| CIC-C7 | Artwork-kind: reticule -> primitive, planet image -> raster ([CXC-CIC-SVG-MAP]) | a test scans a fixture with `reticule` + `planet-image-area` + `planet-resources-graph` and asserts the reticule + resource bars emit native primitives (bullseye/indicators as labeled parts, no bitmap) and the planet image extracts to a CI16/PNG asset | on glass: the reticule + resource bars are crisp at any zoom (vector); the planet image is a raster |
| CIC-C8 | Reticule focus drives the three linked panels from one namespace ([CXC-CIC-CONTENT-PLANET-SURVEY]) | a test publishes `colonial_console/<station>/focus/planet` and asserts the reticule center translates and all three panels (image/resources/description) update from that one namespace; empty -> explicit "no planet focused" state | on glass: focusing a planet moves the reticule and updates all three panels together |
| CIC-C9 | 2-up portrait: two independent stations stack on one display ([CXC-CIC-ASPECT-MULTI]) | a headless render of the 2-up scene asserts two 4:3 instances stack with distinct station scopes and independent frame masks | on glass: a portrait-mounted monitor shows two independent CIC consoles; each drives independently |
| CIC-C10 | Tier stance is recorded, not silent ([CXC-CIC-TIER]) | the spec carries the console/desktop-first stance + reason and an UPHOLDS edge to [CXC-PRIM-TIER-PARITY]; a single reduced console screen is noted as a distinct embedded variant | n/a (structural) |
| CIC-C11 | ONE generalized tab-row, instanced twice with the ratified fills ([CXC-CIC-TABROW]) | a test asserts the SAME tab-row class instanced as row2 (`pill-overlay`, rgba 0x33,0x33,0x33,0xB3) and row3 (`filled-background`, rgba 0x33,0x33,0x33,0xFF); text-bound labels swap per console; a tab tap publishes the station-scoped index, byte-identical to a rotary publish; the indicator derives from the published index (no fork of TabWidget) | on glass: the selected console shows a 70%-opacity #333 pill; the selected sub-tab shows a 100% #333 filled background; labels change with the console |
| CIC-C12 | `theme` is a SEMANTIC binding resolving to a base/highlight palette; the same shell re-themes with no fork ([CXC-CIC-WIDGET] / [DD-CIC-THEME]) | a test binds `theme = sickbay` (a semantic name, not hex) and asserts the shell RESOLVES it to that theme's (`base_color`, `highlight_color`) palette and renders the SAME `standard_ux_shape_element` through ONE code path (no per-theme fork); unbound, `theme` defaults to `cic` -> the amber `#762400` / `#CD671D`; a direct `base_color`/`highlight_color` bind still overrides for a one-off; the artwork is authored at native 1280x960 ([CXC-CIC-ASPECT-MULTI]) and the scan extracts against that reference | on glass: the CIC (`theme=cic`) amber console and a re-themed (e.g. `theme=sickbay`) console are visibly the SAME shell under two semantic theme names |
| CIC-C13 (PROPOSED) | Each radio mode renders content from its OWN svg; absent art -> clean placeholder, never a shared/base group ([CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]) | a test forces the bundled art, publishes `colonial_console/<station>/radio={index:2,key:"EXT"}`, and asserts EXT targets + DRAWS its own `ext-view` group (NOT the generic `screen-scan-stars`, which is byte-identical across `colonial_base_ux.svg`/`ext_mode.svg`); EXT's screen pixels differ from STD's; DRADIS/CHRONO (no art) render a "<MODE> / screen not built" placeholder, never the base stars nor the nav content | on glass (David's verdict): navigating to EXT shows the external-view artwork from `ext_mode.svg` (not the base scan-stars); DRADIS/CHRONO show a clean placeholder until their art is authored |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CIC]

